# UI and design tokens

`src/styles/tokens.css` is the authoritative source for colors, typography, spacing, radii, shadows, motion, z-index, and breakpoints.

Application components must not introduce arbitrary colors, font sizes, or spacing when a token already exists. Add a token when the value is a repeated visual decision, not when it is a one-off implementation detail.

Use semantic token names (`--color-text`, `--space-4`), not raw palette nicknames, in component CSS. Keep product theming out of bootstrap UI; do not design feature screens or the real home screen here.

Prefer CSS modules colocated with the component that owns them. Global styles belong in `src/styles` and should stay limited to reset, root document rules, and token application.

When JS needs breakpoint values, keep them aligned with the numbers documented in `tokens.css`. CSS custom properties cannot reliably drive `@media` queries.
